        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-89",
          "ruleIndex": 1,
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "Unauthenticated SQL injection in product search via string-built raw query.\n\nAttacker-controlled req.query.q (unauthenticated GET /rest/products/search, server.ts:641) is interpolated into a raw SQL string passed to sequelize.query with no parameter binding; the only control is a 200-character truncation at line 22.\n\nImpact: Read of any table in the SQLite database without logging in, including Users (email and MD5 password hashes, see lib/insecurity.ts:41). Write capability depends on the driver and is not claimed here.\n\nExploit scenario: GET /rest/products/search?q= with a payload that closes the LIKE string and appends a UNION SELECT over the Users table or sqlite_master. The rows come back in the JSON body via res.json at line 71. 200 characters is enough for a UNION payload.\n\nPreconditions: None: route is unauthenticated (server.ts:641); unionSqlInjectionChallenge has no disabledEnv (data/static/challenges.yml:1206), so the injectable path is live in every deployment, including Docker and Heroku.\n\nRecommendation: Bind the value instead of concatenating. Also reject non-string q.\n\n  if (typeof req.query.q !== 'string' && req.query.q !== undefined) return res.status(400).json({ error: 'Wrong Params' })\n  const q = typeof req.query.q === 'string' ? req.query.q.slice(0, 200) : ''\n  models.sequelize.query(\n    'SELECT * FROM Products WHERE ((name LIKE :q OR description LIKE :q) AND deletedAt IS NULL) ORDER BY name',\n    { replacements: { q: `%${q}%` } }\n  )\n\nThis removes the intended union challenge behavior, so keep it only on a non-production build if the challenge is wanted.\n\nCWE-89. Severity CRITICAL, confidence high."
          },
