        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-913",
          "ruleIndex": 2,
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "Anonymous registration accepts a client-supplied role, creating admin accounts.\n\nPOST /api/Users is served by finale with excludeAttributes applied only to output (server.ts:543, exclude list at line 523), so the body role reaches UserModel.create, and the role setter (models/user.ts:80-95) accepts admin.\n\nImpact: Unauthenticated creation of admin accounts with full control of catalog, users and orders.\n\nExploit scenario: POST /api/Users with email, password, passwordRepeat and role=admin; log in with the new account and use admin APIs.\n\nPreconditions: none (default configuration).\n\nRecommendation: In the create write hook, rebuild the body: req.body = { email, password, passwordRepeat }; set role to customer; reject role, deluxeToken and profileImage in input. Keep admin creation to an internal seeding path only.\n\nCWE-915. Severity CRITICAL, confidence high."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "server.ts",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 550,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "resource.create.send.before((req: Request, res: Response, context: { instance: { id: any }, continue: any }) => { // vuln-code-snippet vuln-line registerAdminChallenge"
                  }
