        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-287",
          "ruleIndex": 3,
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "Passkey login issues a session even when the assertion did not verify.\n\nloginVerify uses verification.verified only to gate the counter update (line 218) and then calls issuePasskeySession unconditionally on line 222, while loginOptions hands out a victim's credential IDs to any caller who supplies an email. Also CWE-347: loginVerify uses verification.verified only for the counter update (line 218) and a training challenge (line 216). issuePasskeySession runs unconditionally after the lookup by attacker-supplied assertion.id. If verifyAuthenticationResponse returns verified=false for a bad signature (the code's own passkeySignatureChallenge at line 216 assumes it does), the victim's session is still issued. Whether the library returns false rather than throwing was not verified, since node_modules is absent.\n\nImpact: Unauthenticated account takeover of any passkey-enrolled user, including the seeded passkey account.\n\nExploit scenario: POST login-options with the victim email to get a credentialID and authToken, then POST login-verify with an assertion carrying that id, a correct challenge and origin, and a bad signature; a session for the victim is returned.\n\nPreconditions: @simplewebauthn/server returns verified:false rather than throwing on signature mismatch (library not inspected; node_modules absent).\n\nRecommendation: Return 401 when !verification.verified before issuePasskeySession, and bind the assertion to the stored credential's user only after a successful verification. Also CWE-347: Stop issuing the session unless verification succeeded. Patch: if (!verification.verified) { res.status(401).send(res.__('Passkey verification failed.')); return } before the counter update and before issuePasskeySession. If the signature-bypass challenge must remain for training, gate it behind its explicit challenge flag so production builds cannot issue sessions on failed verification.\n\nCWE-287. Severity CRITICAL, confidence medium."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "routes/passkey.ts",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
