        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-347",
          "ruleIndex": 4,
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "JWT verification does not pin the signature algorithm, so HS256 tokens MACed with the public key are accepted.\n\nisAuthorized() builds express-jwt with only a secret (the PEM public key) and no algorithms option, and package.json pins express-jwt 0.1.3 and jsonwebtoken 0.4.0; those versions accept the algorithm named in the attacker's token header, so an HS256 token signed with the public PEM as the HMAC key verifies. The public key is served unauthenticated (routes/keyServer.ts:14 via server.ts:303). Scope note: lib/, with the gated routes in server.ts.\n\nImpact: Forged identities and roles for any user, including admin, without the private key. This survives a key rotation until the libraries are upgraded and the algorithm is pinned.\n\nExploit scenario: Attacker downloads /encryptionkeys/jwt.pub, builds a header {alg:HS256} and payload {data:{role:'admin',...}}, signs it with HMAC-SHA256 keyed by the PEM text, and sends it as a Bearer token. The token passes isAuthorized, isAccounting and updateAuthenticatedUsers.\n\nPreconditions: Network access to the application; node_modules not installed in this review, so library behavior is inferred from the pinned versions and their published advisory history (CVE-2015-9235); not confirmed by execution.\n\nRecommendation: Pin the algorithm everywhere:\\n  export const isAuthorized = () => expressJwt({ secret: publicKey, algorithms: ['RS256'] } as any)\\n  jwt.verify(token, publicKey, { algorithms: ['RS256'] }, cb)\\n  jws.verify(token, 'RS256', publicKey)\\nUpgrade express-jwt (>= 6, whose API is expressjwt({ secret, algorithms })) and jsonwebtoken (>= 9) so that the library enforces the algorithm, and add a regression test that an HS256 token signed with the public key is rejected.\n\nCWE-347. Severity CRITICAL, confidence medium."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "lib/insecurity.ts",
