        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-200",
          "ruleIndex": 5,
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "Unauthenticated GET /rest/memories returns full User rows including password hashes and TOTP secrets.\n\nGET /rest/memories is wired without any auth middleware (server.ts:670). getMemories eager-loads the associated User model with no attributes restriction (MemoryModel.belongsTo(UserModel) at models/relations.ts:78), and line 25 serializes every User column into the response.\n\nImpact: Wholesale credential disclosure for every account that owns a memory. The seeded memories belong to bjoernOwasp and to users named in config memories (john, emma), and any user can create more. Enables password cracking, 2FA bypass and account takeover, plus PII exposure.\n\nExploit scenario: An anonymous client sends GET /rest/memories and receives, for each memory owner, the User object with password (unsalted MD5), totpSecret, email, role, deluxeToken and lastLoginIp. The MD5 hashes are cracked offline and the TOTP secret generates valid second-factor codes, giving account takeover.\n\nPreconditions: None: unauthenticated network request; Affects only users who own at least one memory.\n\nRecommendation: Restrict the join to safe columns: const memories = await MemoryModel.findAll({ attributes: ['id','caption','imagePath','UserId','createdAt'], include: [{ model: UserModel, attributes: ['id','username'] }] }). Rotate the password and TOTP secret of every affected account. Move password hashing off unsalted MD5 (lib/insecurity.ts:41) to bcrypt or argon2. Add a regression test asserting that no password, totpSecret or email keys appear in the response.\n\nCWE-200. Severity HIGH, confidence high."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "routes/memory.ts",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
