        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-200",
          "ruleIndex": 5,
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "Current and new passwords sent in GET query string and written to publicly served access logs.\n\nThe change-password handler reads passwords from the URL query (lines 14-17); morgan('combined') logs every request URL to logs/access.log.<date> (server.ts:362-370), and /support/logs serves that directory and files without authentication (server.ts:306-308). Credentials therefore land in a public file.\n\nImpact: Plaintext credential disclosure to any unauthenticated network client for every user who changed their password in the retention window, including admins. Enables full account takeover.\n\nExploit scenario: Attacker requests /support/logs, opens access.log.<date>, and greps for change-password lines. Each match yields the victim current password and new password in plaintext, enabling login as that user.\n\nPreconditions: Victim used the change-password feature in the last two days (normal use); Access logs are reachable at /support/logs (default configuration).\n\nRecommendation: Move passwords into a POST JSON body:\n\napp.post('/rest/user/change-password', ...)\nconst { current: currentPassword, new: newPassword, repeat: repeatPassword } = req.body\n\nUpdate frontend/src/app/Services/user.service.ts:54 to match. Log without query strings, for example morgan with a custom token that strips req.url after '?'. Remove the public /support/logs mounts (server.ts:306-308) and delete existing access logs.\n\nCWE-598. Severity HIGH, confidence high."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
