        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-918",
          "ruleIndex": 7,
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "Full-response SSRF: server fetches attacker URL and publishes the body at a public path.\n\nreq.body.imageUrl is passed to fetch() (line 24) with no scheme, host, or address restriction, and the response body is written to the public uploads directory (lines 29-30).\n\nImpact: Read of internal HTTP services and cloud metadata reachable from the server, with the body exfiltrated through the public static path. Any response body is accepted regardless of content type.\n\nExploit scenario: POST /profile/image/url with imageUrl set to http://169.254.169.254/... or an internal admin URL. The response body is saved as frontend/dist/.../uploads/<id>.jpg and served publicly at /assets/public/images/uploads/<id>.jpg, so the attacker reads it anonymously.\n\nPreconditions: Any registered account (cookie token must map to a logged-in user, line 21); No challenge gating.\n\nRecommendation: Restrict the target: parse with new URL(), allow only http and https, resolve the hostname and reject loopback, RFC1918, link-local 169.254.0.0/16, and ULA addresses, fetch with redirect manual, and require a content-type starting with image/ plus a size cap before writing.\n\n  const target = new URL(url)\n  if (!['http:', 'https:'].includes(target.protocol)) throw new Error('Unsupported URL')\n  // resolve target.hostname, reject private ranges\n  const response = await fetch(target, { redirect: 'manual' }).\n\nCWE-918. Severity HIGH, confidence high."
          },
