          "ruleId": "CWE-1284",
          "ruleIndex": 9,
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "Client-supplied amount credits the wallet; the only payment check is card ownership.\n\naddWalletBalance checks only that a card with the given id belongs to the caller (line 24). It then credits req.body.balance, which is never validated or tied to any charge. Store credit is later spent by routes/order.ts:147-150 when paymentId is 'wallet'. Also CWE-20: addWalletBalance checks only that the posted card id belongs to the caller (line 24) and then increments the wallet by req.body.balance on line 27, with no payment capture.\n\nImpact: Unlimited store credit and free purchases. Direct financial loss for the shop with no payment taken.\n\nExploit scenario: Registered user creates their own card record via POST /api/Cards, then sends PUT /rest/wallet/balance with {\"paymentId\": <their card id>, \"balance\": 1000000}. The wallet is credited with no charge. The user then checks out with orderDetails.paymentId = 'wallet' for free.\n\nPreconditions: Registered account; A card record, which the user can create through /api/Cards.\n\nRecommendation: Remove the client-controlled amount. Top-ups must come from a payment-provider transaction whose confirmed amount is what gets credited. Interim patch: accept only server-defined top-up amounts (for example const TOPUP_AMOUNTS = [10, 20, 50]; reject anything else with 400), and perform the charge and the credit in one transaction. Also CWE-20: Remove client-controlled crediting. Credit only from a verified payment result, and bound the amount server-side (positive, capped).\n\nCWE-1284. Severity HIGH, confidence high."
          },
