          "ruleId": "CWE-22",
          "ruleIndex": 10,
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "Zip-slip: archive entry paths are written outside the upload directory.\n\nentry.path from an unauthenticated zip (line 30) is concatenated into the write path on line 34, and the only containment test (line 33) checks that the absolute path contains the project root string, which does not confine writes.\n\nImpact: Arbitrary file overwrite under the app root, persistent XSS for every user, and code change on restart.\n\nExploit scenario: A zip entry such as ../../../../<path containing the app root>/frontend/dist/frontend/index.html overwrites a publicly served asset, giving persistent XSS to all visitors; config or data files can be overwritten the same way.\n\nPreconditions: non-Docker/Heroku runtime: fileWriteChallenge has disabledEnv Docker/Heroku under safetyMode auto.\n\nRecommendation: const base = path.resolve('uploads/complaints'); const target = path.resolve(base, entry.path); if (!target.startsWith(base + path.sep)) throw new Error('Invalid path'); then write to target; also skip directory and symlink entries.\n\nCWE-22. Severity HIGH, confidence high."
