          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "Coupons are unsigned z85 strings, so any user can mint an arbitrary discount.\n\napplyCoupon accepts the coupon from the URL (line 14) and passes it to discountFromCoupon, which only z85-decodes it and checks the current month, with no signature or server-side record.\n\nImpact: Financial loss from arbitrary discounts on any order.\n\nExploit scenario: z85-encode the current MMMYY-99, PUT /rest/basket/:id/coupon/<code>, then check out to receive a 99% discount.\n\nPreconditions: authenticated account.\n\nRecommendation: Sign coupons with an HMAC over code, discount and expiry using a server secret, store issued codes server-side, reject unsigned values, and cap discounts on the server.\n\nCWE-345. Severity HIGH, confidence high."
          },
