        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-345",
          "ruleIndex": 11,
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "Coupon is only z85-encoded, not authenticated, so any user can mint a discount of any size.\n\ndiscountFromCoupon decodes the client-supplied coupon with z85.decode (line 106). z85 is a reversible encoding with no key. The string is accepted when it matches MMMYY-N for the current month (lines 107-111), and the returned value is parseInt of N with no upper or lower bound (line 112). routes/coupon.ts:15 passes the attacker's :coupon path parameter straight in; applyCoupon stores it on the basket (coupon.ts:24) and placeOrder re-derives and applies it (order.ts:191, then order.ts:113-118). PUT /rest/basket/:id/coupon/:coupon is behind isAuthorized (server.ts:431), so a registered account is enough. The repo's forgedCouponChallenge hook (order.ts:193) shows the forgery is anticipated, but the flaw is real regardless.\n\nImpact: Arbitrary price manipulation: free orders and negative order totals for any authenticated user, and wallet credit when combined with wallet payment and a chosen UserId. This is an integrity loss on pricing and balances.\n\nExploit scenario: A registered user encodes the string '<current MMMYY>-100' (for example NOV26-100 in November 2026) with z85 and sends PUT /rest/basket/<own id>/coupon/<encoded>. Checkout then applies 100 percent, so totalPrice becomes 0. With N greater than 100, totalPrice becomes negative. If paymentId is 'wallet', order.ts:148-150 checks wallet.balance >= totalPrice (true for negative values) and calls WalletModel.decrement with a negative amount, which credits the wallet. The UserId in req.body is not bound to the session on checkout, so the credit can target any user id.\n\nPreconditions: Authenticated account (the coupon route sits behind isAuthorized); Coupon must name the current calendar month (the validity check compares against today's MMMYY).\n\nRecommendation: Issue coupons server-side and authenticate them. In lib/insecurity.ts, sign the payload with an HMAC over a dedicated secret and compare in constant time: export const generateCoupon = (discount: number, date = new Date()) => { const body = utils.toMMMYY(date) + '-' + discount; const mac = crypto.createHmac('sha256', process.env.COUPON_HMAC_KEY ?? '').update(body).digest('hex'); return z85.encode(body + '.' + mac) }. In discountFromCoupon, split body and mac, recompute, check lengths equal before crypto.timingSafeEqual, check MMMYY, and return the discount only if it is an integer from 1 to 100. Better still, keep issued coupons in a table with validity and single-use state and look them up by code. Also reject totalPrice < 0 in placeOrder before any wallet operation, and bind UserId from the session with appendUserId on checkout.\n\nCWE-345. Severity HIGH, confidence high."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "lib/insecurity.ts",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 112,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "return parseInt(discount)"
                  }
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "discountFromCoupon",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "discountFromCoupon"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "claudeSecurityPlugin": {
              "id": "F17",
              "title": "Coupon is only z85-encoded, not authenticated, so any user can mint a discount of any size",
              "impact": "Arbitrary price manipulation: free orders and negative order totals for any authenticated user, and wallet credit when combined with wallet payment and a chosen UserId. This is an integrity loss on pricing and balances.",
              "file": "lib/insecurity.ts",
              "line": 112,
              "description": "discountFromCoupon decodes the client-supplied coupon with z85.decode (line 106). z85 is a reversible encoding with no key. The string is accepted when it matches MMMYY-N for the current month (lines 107-111), and the returned value is parseInt of N with no upper or lower bound (line 112). routes/coupon.ts:15 passes the attacker's :coupon path parameter straight in; applyCoupon stores it on the basket (coupon.ts:24) and placeOrder re-derives and applies it (order.ts:191, then order.ts:113-118). PUT /rest/basket/:id/coupon/:coupon is behind isAuthorized (server.ts:431), so a registered account is enough. The repo's forgedCouponChallenge hook (order.ts:193) shows the forgery is anticipated, but the flaw is real regardless.",
              "exploit_scenario": "A registered user encodes the string '<current MMMYY>-100' (for example NOV26-100 in November 2026) with z85 and sends PUT /rest/basket/<own id>/coupon/<encoded>. Checkout then applies 100 percent, so totalPrice becomes 0. With N greater than 100, totalPrice becomes negative. If paymentId is 'wallet', order.ts:148-150 checks wallet.balance >= totalPrice (true for negative values) and calls WalletModel.decrement with a negative amount, which credits the wallet. The UserId in req.body is not bound to the session on checkout, so the credit can target any user id.",
              "preconditions": [
                "Authenticated account (the coupon route sits behind isAuthorized)",
                "Coupon must name the current calendar month (the validity check compares against today's MMMYY)"
              ],
              "category": "Insufficient Verification of Data Authenticity",
              "severity": "HIGH",
              "confidence": "high",
              "recommendation": "Issue coupons server-side and authenticate them. In lib/insecurity.ts, sign the payload with an HMAC over a dedicated secret and compare in constant time: export const generateCoupon = (discount: number, date = new Date()) => { const body = utils.toMMMYY(date) + '-' + discount; const mac = crypto.createHmac('sha256', process.env.COUPON_HMAC_KEY ?? '').update(body).digest('hex'); return z85.encode(body + '.' + mac) }. In discountFromCoupon, split body and mac, recompute, check lengths equal before crypto.timingSafeEqual, check MMMYY, and return the discount only if it is an integer from 1 to 100. Better still, keep issued coupons in a table with validity and single-use state and look them up by code. Also reject totalPrice < 0 in placeOrder before any wallet operation, and bind UserId from the session with appendUserId on checkout.",
              "cwe_id": "CWE-345",
              "snippet": "return parseInt(discount)",
              "symbol": "discountFromCoupon",
              "declared_line": 112,
              "via_change": null,
              "other_cwe_ids": [],
