          "ruleId": "CWE-798",
          "ruleIndex": 0,
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "Seed data ships plaintext default passwords for the admin and other accounts, plus a TOTP seed.\n\nThe seed file stores plaintext passwords for the admin and many other accounts (users.yml lines 3-296) and a TOTP secret for a seeded account (line 151), which the server uses to create live accounts on every fresh install.\n\nImpact: Admin takeover on default installs and account takeover for every seeded user.\n\nExploit scenario: On a default deployment, log in as admin@juice-sh.op with the seeded password; with the password and the TOTP seed, 2FA is also defeated for that account.\n\nPreconditions: default seed data used (the normal first-run state).\n\nRecommendation: Remove literal passwords from the seed. Generate random credentials per install at first boot or force a setup step, hash them at seed time, rotate the TOTP seed, and document that the seed is not for production.\n\nThe source line is not quoted because it holds the credential.\n\nCWE-798. Severity HIGH, confidence high."
