          "ruleId": "CWE-22",
          "ruleIndex": 10,
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "Unauthenticated arbitrary file read via backslash traversal on Windows in log route.\n\nparams.file is checked only for forward slashes (line 13), and on Windows path.resolve treats backslash as a separator, so the path escapes logs/ with no extension restriction. Also CWE-532: serveLogFiles sends any logs/ file without authentication, and morgan writes full request URLs, including the query strings that carry current and new passwords, into those logs.\n\nImpact: Unauthenticated read of any file readable by the Node process on Windows hosts.\n\nExploit scenario: GET /support/logs/ with a file parameter of ..\\..\\config\\default.yml (URL-encoded backslashes) returns that file from the host filesystem.\n\nPreconditions: Server running on Windows; No authentication (server.ts:308).\n\nRecommendation: Same confinement as the quarantine route: reject backslashes and non-basename input, resolve against logs/, check startsWith(base + path.sep), then sendFile the resolved path. Also CWE-532: Stop logging sensitive URLs: use a morgan token that redacts or omits the query string for auth routes, or log req.path only. Move change-password to POST with a JSON body. Restrict /support/logs and /ftp listings to authenticated admins. Purge existing logs and rotate exposed passwords.\n\nCWE-22. Severity HIGH, confidence medium."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "routes/logfileServer.ts",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 14,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "res.sendFile(path.resolve('logs/', file))"
                  }
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "serveLogFiles",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "serveLogFiles"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
