          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "TLS private key committed in Terraform (same RSA key as the JWT signer).\n\naws_iam_server_certificate sets private_key to an RSA private key literal on line 171; the same key also appears at terraform/networking.tf:171 and in lib/insecurity.ts:21.\n\nImpact: TLS impersonation or MITM for the deployed endpoint, plus key reuse with the JWT signer.\n\nExploit scenario: With the key, an attacker who controls network position can impersonate the TLS endpoint, and the same key forges session tokens as described for lib/insecurity.ts:21.\n\nPreconditions: network position for MITM (for the TLS impact).\n\nRecommendation: Revoke and reissue the certificate and key, reference the key from a secret store or ACM rather than a literal, purge it from git history, and stop reusing one key for TLS and JWT.\n\nThe source line is not quoted because it holds the credential.\n\nCWE-321. Severity HIGH, confidence medium."
