          "ruleId": "CWE-94",
          "ruleIndex": 8,
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "Pug template injection: raw username spliced into template source enables server-side code execution via newline-led '-' lines.\n\nThe attacker-chosen username is inserted raw into the pug template source at line 73, and pug.compile at line 90 compiles it, so newline-led unbuffered-code lines execute as JavaScript.\n\nImpact: Arbitrary code execution as the server process through the template engine, equivalent to the eval finding. A separate route to the same impact.\n\nExploit scenario: Register an account and log in. POST /profile with urlencoded body username=%0A-%20global.process.mainModule.require('child_process').execSync('id'). The stored value starts with a newline, so after the backslash prefix a line begins with '- ' at column 0 inside the pug source. pug compiles that as unbuffered JavaScript and runs it when GET /profile renders. This path does not need the #{...} form used for the eval finding. Plain pug text is also emitted unescaped, so the same injection gives stored XSS in the attacker's own profile page.\n\nPreconditions: usernameXssChallenge enabled (not Docker or Heroku, safetyMode auto or enabled); An authenticated session via open self-registration.\n\nRecommendation: Never splice user data into template source. Use the same patch as the eval finding: keep template.replace(/_username_/g, '#{username}') unconditionally, and pass username as a pug local (fn({ username, ... })). As defence in depth, reject control characters in username in routes/updateUserProfile.ts before user.update, for example if (/[\\u0000-\\u001f\\u007f]/.test(req.body.username)) return res.status(400).end(). Newlines are the characters that enable the unbuffered-code break-out.\n\nCWE-1336. Severity HIGH, confidence medium."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "routes/userProfile.ts",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 73,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "template = template.replace(/_username_/g, username)"
                  }
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "getUserProfile",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "getUserProfile"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "claudeSecurityPlugin": {
