        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-639",
          "ruleIndex": 6,
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "Passkey registration overwrites another user's credential (no ownership check).\n\nregisterVerify looks up an existing passkey by credentialID alone. When a row is found, it overwrites that row's publicKey, counter, transports and aaguid (lines 142-146) without checking existing.UserId against the caller. An authenticated attacker can take over a victim's credential. The attack assumes the attacker can produce a registration response with a chosen credential ID, which is feasible with attestationType 'none' but not verified by execution.\n\nImpact: Persistent passkey-based account takeover of victim accounts, which survives password resets because the passkey stays bound to the attacker's key.\n\nExploit scenario: Attacker registers an account, obtains the victim's credentialID from POST /rest/passkey/login-options with the victim email, and builds a registration response (attestation 'none') whose credential ID equals the victim's and whose public key is the attacker's. POST /rest/passkey/register-verify overwrites the victim's passkey row. The attacker then signs in as the victim through login-verify with the matching private key.\n\nPreconditions: Attacker has a registered account (required by isAuthorized at server.ts:510); Victim has an enrolled passkey and its credentialID is discoverable through login-options; Attacker can produce a registration response with a chosen credential ID.\n\nRecommendation: Scope the lookup to the caller and reject foreign credentials. Patch: const existing = await PasskeyModel.findOne({ where: { credentialID } }); if (existing && existing.UserId !== user.id) { res.status(409).json({ error: 'credential already registered' }); return }. Also add a unique index on credentialID in the model and stop returning credentialIDs for arbitrary emails from login-options.\n\nCWE-639. Severity HIGH, confidence medium."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "routes/passkey.ts",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 140,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "const existing = await PasskeyModel.findOne({ where: { credentialID } })"
                  }
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "registerVerify",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "registerVerify"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "claudeSecurityPlugin": {
