          "ruleId": "CWE-307",
          "ruleIndex": 13,
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "Reset-password rate limit keyed on client-controlled X-Forwarded-For, enabling unlimited security-answer guessing.\n\napp.enable('trust proxy') (server.ts:374) makes req.ip the left-most X-Forwarded-For entry, which the client sets. The keyGenerator reads headers['X-Forwarded-For'] (capitalised, so always undefined in Node) and falls back to ip. Each request with a fresh spoofed XFF therefore gets a new bucket. routes/resetPassword.ts:41 compares the security answer with no per-account lockout, so guessing is unbounded.\n\nImpact: Account takeover for any account whose security answer is guessable from a dictionary, with no victim interaction.\n\nExploit scenario: Attacker confirms a victim email via GET /rest/user/security-question?email=. They then loop POST /rest/user/reset-password with {email, answer: <dictionary word>, new, repeat} and a random X-Forwarded-For value on each request. The per-IP limit never triggers. On a hit, resetPassword.ts:44 sets the new password.\n\nPreconditions: Victim security answer is guessable; Victim email is known or enumerable.\n\nRecommendation: Do not trust client-supplied forwarding headers. Set trust proxy to the exact number of real proxy hops (not true) and key the limiter on req.ip, or on req.socket.remoteAddress when no proxy is present. Patch: app.set('trust proxy', 1); app.use('/rest/user/reset-password', rateLimit({ windowMs: 5*60*1000, max: 100, keyGenerator: (req) => req.ip ?? 'unknown' })). Separately, add a per-email failed-answer counter in resetPassword.ts with a lockout or backoff, since per-IP limits alone cannot stop distributed guessing.\n\nCWE-307. Severity HIGH, confidence medium."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "server.ts",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 378,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "keyGenerator ({ headers, ip }: { headers: any, ip: any }) { return headers['X-Forwarded-For'] ?? ip }"
                  }
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "configureApp",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "configureApp"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
