          "ruleId": "CWE-20",
          "ruleIndex": 12,
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "Negative quantity accepted, enabling wallet credit via negative order total.\n\nreq.body.quantity flows from quantityCheckBeforeBasketItemAddition (basketItems.ts:60) and quantityCheckBeforeBasketItemUpdate (basketItems.ts:75-76) into quantityCheck with no lower bound. At line 94, the first clause !product.limitPerUser is true whenever the limit is null, and product.quantity >= quantity (line 95) is true for any negative value, so negative quantities always pass and are persisted (basketItems.ts:40-47). At checkout, order.ts:93 computes itemTotal = itemPrice * BasketItem.quantity, which becomes negative, and totalPrice goes negative (order.ts:106, 133). order.ts:149 then passes wallet.balance >= totalPrice, and order.ts:150 calls WalletModel.decrement({ balance: totalPrice }), which with a negative amount increases the balance.\n\nImpact: Unbounded creation of store-wallet balance by any registered user (integrity of the stored value), plus negative-total order records and inflated stock counts (order.ts:78-81). Intentional in the training app (negativeOrderChallenge, order.ts:144), but the flaw is real and reachable.\n\nExploit scenario: Register, then POST /api/BasketItems with {\"ProductId\":1,\"BasketId\":<own basket>,\"quantity\":-1000}. Then POST /rest/basket/<own basket>/checkout with orderDetails.paymentId 'wallet'. The wallet is credited by price*1000 and can be spent on real orders. The same negative-quantity bypass applies to PUT /api/BasketItems/:id via quantityCheckBeforeBasketItemUpdate.\n\nPreconditions: Any registered account. Self-registration is open, and a Wallet row is created at registration (server.ts:551), so this is not a privileged attacker.; The attacker pays with paymentId 'wallet' (order.ts:147).\n\nRecommendation: Validate quantity at the entry point and again before any wallet operation.\n\nasync function quantityCheck (req, res, next, id, quantity) {\n  const qty = Number(quantity)\n  if (!Number.isInteger(qty) || qty < 1) {\n    res.status(400).json({ error: 'Quantity must be a positive integer.' })\n    return\n  }\n  // ...existing checks unchanged\n}\n\nIn order.ts placeOrder, reject non-positive totals before the stock update loop (lines 78-82) and before any wallet call (line 146):\n\nif (totalPrice < 0) { next(new Error('Invalid order total.')); return }.\n\nCWE-20. Severity HIGH, confidence medium."
          },
