          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Any authenticated user can list every account (emails, roles, deluxeToken, last-login IPs).\n\nThe route is guarded only by security.isAuthorized() (server.ts:430, which accepts any valid JWT), so a customer token passes. The handler has no role check, selects every UserModel row, and spreads all dataValues into the response. Only password and totpSecret are masked, and deluxeToken and lastLoginIp are returned in clear.\n\nImpact: Mass disclosure of all users' personal data and roles to any registered customer. The deluxeToken and role data also help target privilege escalation. Masked password and TOTP fields still leak length and 2FA status.\n\nExploit scenario: Register a normal account, log in, then send GET /rest/user/authentication-details with Authorization: Bearer <token>. The response lists every user with email, role, deluxeToken, lastLoginIp, profileImage and lastLoginTime, which identifies admin and accounting accounts for targeting.\n\nPreconditions: Any registered account (self-service registration).\n\nRecommendation: Enforce admin role inside the handler and restrict the projection. Patch: const caller = security.authenticatedUsers.from(req); if (caller?.data?.role !== security.roles.admin) { res.status(403).json({ status: 'error', error: 'Forbidden' }); return }. Then call UserModel.findAll({ attributes: ['id', 'username', 'email', 'role', 'lastLoginIp', 'profileImage'] }) and drop deluxeToken, password and totpSecret from the response.\n\nCWE-862. Severity MEDIUM, confidence high."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "routes/authenticatedUsers.ts",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
