        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-532",
          "ruleIndex": 17,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Access log download exposes plaintext passwords from GET change-password query strings.\n\nThe UI sends current and new passwords as query parameters to GET /rest/user/change-password (frontend/src/app/Services/user.service.ts:54; routes/changePassword.ts:14-17), and morgan 'combined' writes the full URL into logs/access.log.<date> (server.ts:362-370). /support/logs and /support/logs/:file are mounted with no authentication (server.ts:305-308), so an anonymous user can download the log. Scope note: the logging and exposure glue is in server.ts.\n\nImpact: Plaintext credentials of users who recently changed passwords are disclosed to anonymous users, enabling account takeover. Client IPs and emails carried in query strings are also exposed. The log exposure is an intentional accessLogDisclosure challenge, but the password leakage is an unintended defect.\n\nExploit scenario: Attacker requests /support/logs, reads the directory listing, and downloads access.log.<date>. Each line for a UI password change contains the user's old and new password in plaintext, which the attacker uses to take over the account.\n\nPreconditions: At least one user changed their password through the UI within the two-day log retention window.\n\nRecommendation: Stop logging credentials and require authorization for log downloads:\\n  morgan.token('url-redacted', (req: any) => (req.originalUrl ?? req.url).replace(/([?&](current|new|repeat)=)[^&]*/gi, '$1REDACTED'))\\n  app.use(morgan(':remote-addr - :remote-user [:date[clf]] \\\":method :url-redacted HTTP/:http-version\\\" :status :res[content-length] \\\":referrer\\\" \\\":user-agent\\\"', { stream: accessLogStream }))\\nGate the log routes with security.isAccounting() or an admin check, and move the password change to a POST with a JSON body. Purge existing logs and rotate any password that appears in them.\n\nCWE-532. Severity MEDIUM, confidence high."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "server.ts",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 308,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "  app.use('/support/logs/:file', serveLogFiles()) // vuln-code-snippet vuln-line accessLogDisclosureChallenge"
                  }
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "configureApp",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "configureApp"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
