        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-639",
          "ruleIndex": 6,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "PUT /api/Addresss/:id has no ownership check, allowing takeover of other users' address records.\n\nThe PUT route only runs appendUserId(), which sets req.body.UserId to the caller, and then falls through to the finale-generated update that loads the Address by primary key with no owner filter (server.ts:532, 540-546); GET and DELETE by id filter by UserId in routes/address.ts:18 and :29, but PUT is left to finale. Scope note: the sink is server.ts glue.\n\nImpact: Cross-user write and read of personal addresses (names, phone numbers, street addresses) for all users. The attacker can also overwrite victims' shipping data, which affects future orders.\n\nExploit scenario: Attacker registers a free account, enumerates sequential Address ids, sends PUT /api/Addresss/<victimId> with an empty body or UserId, which reassigns the record to the attacker. GET /api/Addresss then returns the victim's name, phone, street, zip and city.\n\nPreconditions: Any authenticated customer account (free self-registration).\n\nRecommendation: Add an ownership check before the finale update:\\n  app.put('/api/Addresss/:id', security.appendUserId(), utils.asyncHandler(async (req, res, next) => {\\n    const owned = await AddressModel.findOne({ where: { id: req.params.id, UserId: req.body.UserId } })\\n    if (owned == null) return res.status(400).json({ status: 'error', data: 'Malicious activity detected.' })\\n    next()\\n  }))\\nAlso strip UserId from the body for updates so ownership cannot be transferred.\n\nCWE-639. Severity MEDIUM, confidence high."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "server.ts",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 482,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "  app.put('/api/Addresss/:id', security.appendUserId())"
                  }
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "configureApp",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "configureApp"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "claudeSecurityPlugin": {
