        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-200",
          "ruleIndex": 5,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Any authenticated user receives every account record, including emails, roles and deluxe tokens.\n\nGET /rest/user/authentication-details requires only a valid token (server.ts:430), and retrieveUserList spreads ...user.dataValues for all users on line 25.\n\nImpact: Mass PII disclosure and enumeration of privileged accounts for targeting.\n\nExploit scenario: Any customer requests /rest/user/authentication-details and receives all accounts with email, role, lastLoginIp and deluxeToken.\n\nPreconditions: any registered account.\n\nRecommendation: Require security.isAccounting() or an admin role, return an allowlist of fields (id, email, username, role), and drop deluxeToken and lastLoginIp from list responses.\n\nCWE-200. Severity MEDIUM, confidence high."
