        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-287",
          "ruleIndex": 3,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Password change does not require the current password when it is omitted.\n\nThe current-password check is short-circuited by 'currentPassword &&'. If current is absent or empty, the password is replaced with no proof of knowledge. A stolen bearer token alone is therefore enough to permanently change the password.\n\nImpact: Session-only compromise becomes persistent account takeover. Sessions are not revoked on password change.\n\nExploit scenario: With a stolen Authorization token (for example from XSS or a leaked log), the attacker sends GET /rest/user/change-password?new=X&repeat=X. The password changes and the victim is locked out, so the access survives token expiry.\n\nPreconditions: A valid session token for the victim.\n\nRecommendation: Always require the current password and fail closed: if (!currentPassword || security.hash(currentPassword) !== loggedInUser.data.password) { res.status(401).send(res.__('Current password is not correct.')); return }. Also revoke the account's other tokens on password change.\n\nCWE-620. Severity MEDIUM, confidence high."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "routes/changePassword.ts",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 39,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "if (currentPassword && security.hash(currentPassword) !== loggedInUser.data.password) {"
                  }
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "changePassword",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "changePassword"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "claudeSecurityPlugin": {
              "id": "F34",
              "title": "Password change does not require the current password when it is omitted",
              "impact": "Session-only compromise becomes persistent account takeover. Sessions are not revoked on password change.",
              "file": "routes/changePassword.ts",
