          "ruleId": "CWE-601",
          "ruleIndex": 19,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Open redirect: substring allowlist check accepts attacker-controlled hosts.\n\nquery.to reaches res.redirect after isRedirectAllowed, which uses url.includes(allowedUrl) (lib/insecurity.ts:136), so any URL that contains an allowlisted string passes.\n\nImpact: Redirection of victims from a trusted origin to attacker-controlled sites (phishing). No direct server compromise.\n\nExploit scenario: Send a victim https://attacker.example/?https://github.com/juice-shop/juice-shop, which passes the includes() check and redirects to the attacker host from the trusted domain. Used for phishing.\n\nPreconditions: Victim must follow the attacker-crafted link; redirectChallenge is not disabled in any environment.\n\nRecommendation: Replace the substring test with exact membership:\n\n  if (security.redirectAllowlist.has(toUrl)) { res.redirect(toUrl) } else { res.status(406); next(...) }\n\nIn lib/insecurity.ts:136 this means allowed = redirectAllowlist.has(url). If prefix matching is needed, parse with new URL() and compare origin and pathname.\n\nCWE-601. Severity MEDIUM, confidence high."
          },
