        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-639",
          "ruleIndex": 6,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Any authenticated user can edit any other user's product review (no ownership check).\n\nPATCH /rest/products/reviews requires only isAuthorized (server.ts:674). The handler computes the caller (line 16) but selects the target review solely by the client-supplied req.body.id (line 18) and writes req.body.message (line 19). The caller identity is used only to score a challenge (line 24), never to enforce ownership. Also CWE-943: PATCH /rest/products/reviews (server.ts:674) requires only a valid token, and req.body.id on line 18 can be an operator object combined with multi:true on line 20, with no check that the caller authored the review.\n\nImpact: Integrity loss on other users' review content across the catalogue. The multi:true flag combined with a raw _id from the body could widen the write to more documents if the datastore accepts operator objects. That was not verified because marsdb is not installed.\n\nExploit scenario: An attacker self-registers, reads review _id values from the unauthenticated GET /rest/products/:id/reviews (showProductReviews), and PATCHes another customer's review with phishing text or defacement.\n\nPreconditions: Any registered account (self-registration is open).\n\nRecommendation: Make the handler async and enforce ownership: const user = security.authenticatedUsers.from(req); const id = typeof req.body.id === 'string' ? req.body.id : undefined; if (!user || !id || typeof req.body.message !== 'string') return res.status(400).json({ error: 'Bad request' }); const review = await db.reviewsCollection.findOne({ _id: id }); if (!review) return res.status(404).json({ error: 'Not found' }); if (review.author !== user.data.email) return res.status(403).json({ error: 'Not allowed' }); const result = await db.reviewsCollection.update({ _id: id }, { $set: { message: req.body.message } }); res.json(result). Drop multi:true. This removes the forgedReviewChallenge hook. Also CWE-943: Reject non-string id, add author: user.data.email to the filter, and drop multi: true.\n\nCWE-639. Severity MEDIUM, confidence high."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "routes/updateProductReviews.ts",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 18,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "      { _id: req.body.id }, // vuln-code-snippet vuln-line noSqlReviewsChallenge forgedReviewChallenge"
                  }
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "updateProductReviews",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "updateProductReviews"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
