              ],
              "category": "Interpretation Conflict",
              "severity": "MEDIUM",
              "confidence": "high",
              "recommendation": "Use one parsed value for both the check and the write. Drop the streaming parser from this handler and use the already-parsed body (last key wins, same as the rest of the app), or reject bodies containing duplicate keys:\n\nexport function addBasketItem () {\n  return async (req: Request, res: Response, next: NextFunction) => {\n    const user = security.authenticatedUsers.from(req)\n    const { ProductId, BasketId, quantity } = req.body\n    if (user && BasketId !== undefined && Number(user.bid) !== Number(BasketId)) {\n      res.status(401).send('{\\'error\\' : \\'Invalid BasketId\\'}')\n      return\n    }\n    const basketItem = { ProductId, BasketId, quantity }\n    // keep the basketManipulateChallenge hook and the save logic\n  }\n}\n\nAlso reject non-object request bodies, so a text body cannot skip the check. Also CWE-639: Validate and persist the same value. Reject any body with more than one BasketId key, then compare the single value to user.bid: `if (basketIds.length > 1) return res.status(400).send('duplicate BasketId'); const bid = Number(basketIds[0]); if (user && bid !== Number(user.bid)) return res.status(401).send(...)`. Persist the validated bid rather than the last parsed value.",
