        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-639",
          "ruleIndex": 6,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Any authenticated user can read any basket by numeric id (IDOR).\n\nretrieveBasket looks up the basket only by req.params.id and never checks UserId. The /rest/basket guard (server.ts:388) only requires login, and the sole check at basket.ts:21-25 is a challenge hook that does not block. The response includes the basket's UserId, coupon and product list. Basket IDs are sequential. The check looks deliberate (basketAccessChallenge), but the authorization gap is real.\n\nImpact: Disclosure of other users' cart contents, coupons and account identifiers.\n\nExploit scenario: A logged-in customer requests GET /rest/basket/1, 2, 3, ... and reads other customers' baskets, including their UserId, coupon and products.\n\nPreconditions: Any registered account (self-registration is open).\n\nRecommendation: Add the owner to the query and return 404 on mismatch. req.body.UserId is already set server-side by appendUserId. Patch: `const basket = await BasketModel.findOne({ where: { id, UserId: req.body.UserId }, include: [...] }); if (!basket) return res.status(404).json({ status: 'error', data: 'Not found' })`.\n\nCWE-639. Severity MEDIUM, confidence high."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "routes/basket.ts",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 19,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "const basket = await BasketModel.findOne({ where: { id }, include: [{ model: ProductModel, paranoid: false, as: 'Products' }] })"
                  }
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "retrieveBasket",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "retrieveBasket"
                }
