        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-639",
          "ruleIndex": 6,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Checkout looks up the basket by id with no owner check, so any user can check out and wipe another user's cart.\n\nplaceOrder loads the basket by req.params.id only. The buyer is the authenticated requester, so the purchase, wallet debit and order are charged to the attacker, while basket.update({coupon:null}) and BasketItemModel.destroy({where:{BasketId:id}}) act on the victim's basket (order.ts:50-51).\n\nImpact: Victim's cart is consumed and destroyed, and goods are obtained under the attacker's account. Confidentiality is not affected.\n\nExploit scenario: Attacker POSTs /rest/basket/<victim basket id>/checkout with their own paymentId and addressId. The victim's items are bought under the attacker's account and the victim's cart is emptied.\n\nPreconditions: Any registered account; Victim basket id is known or guessable (sequential).\n\nRecommendation: Scope the lookup to the requester and return 404 otherwise. Patch: `BasketModel.findOne({ where: { id, UserId: req.body.UserId }, include: [...] })` and respond 404 when null.\n\nCWE-639. Severity MEDIUM, confidence high."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "routes/order.ts",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
