        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-770",
          "ruleIndex": 22,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Unauthenticated multipart upload writes unbounded files to disk before the auth check.\n\nThe multer disk storage on /rest/memories has no size limit (server.ts:740-759) and writes the body to the publicly served uploads directory before security.appendUserId() rejects anonymous callers (server.ts:344). Scope note: the upload middleware is in server.ts. Also CWE-400: POST /rest/memories runs uploadToDisk (no limits configured) before security.appendUserId rejects anonymous callers, so files persist even for requests that are refused.\n\nImpact: Disk exhaustion denial of service for anonymous attackers. Arbitrary image-typed content is also hosted under the public uploads path.\n\nExploit scenario: Anonymous client sends many large multipart requests with image/png or image/jpeg as the part mimetype. Multer streams each to frontend/dist/frontend/assets/public/images/uploads/ and then appendUserId returns 401, but the files are not removed, so the disk fills up.\n\nPreconditions: Default configuration; no authentication required.\n\nRecommendation: Authenticate before reading the body and cap sizes:\\n  app.post('/rest/memories', security.isAuthorized(), uploadToDisk.single('image'), ensureFileIsPassed, security.appendUserId(), ...)\\nWith uploadToDisk = multer({ storage: ..., limits: { fileSize: 200000 } }). Delete the temporary file when a later step rejects the request, and check magic bytes. Also CWE-400: Move security.appendUserId() before the multer middleware and add limits: { fileSize } to the multer configuration.\n\nCWE-770. Severity MEDIUM, confidence high."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "server.ts",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 344,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "  app.post('/rest/memories', uploadToDisk.single('image'), ensureFileIsPassed, security.appendUserId(), metrics.observeFileUploadMetricsMiddleware(), utils.asyncHandler(addMemory()))"
                  }
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "configureApp",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "configureApp"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "claudeSecurityPlugin": {
