        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-307",
          "ruleIndex": 13,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Password login has no throttling or lockout (no rate limiter mounted on /rest/user/login).\n\nThe rejection branch returns 401 with no failure counter, lockout or delay. The only rate limiters in the app are at server.ts:375, 491, 498 and 504 (reset-password, 2FA verify, setup and disable), and none covers /rest/user/login. Passwords are unsalted MD5 (lib/insecurity.ts:41), so a weak password falls quickly to unlimited online guessing.\n\nImpact: Account takeover of weak-password accounts through online guessing and credential stuffing.\n\nExploit scenario: Attacker uses a known or enumerated email (from public reviews, which show author emails) and runs a password list against POST /rest/user/login with no limit. Any account with a weak password is taken over.\n\nPreconditions: Target has a weak or reused password; Network access to the login endpoint.\n\nRecommendation: Mount a limiter on /rest/user/login keyed on the normalized email plus the IP, not IP alone, with exponential backoff or temporary lockout after repeated failures. Example: app.post('/rest/user/login', rateLimit({ windowMs: 15*60*1000, max: 10, validate: false, keyGenerator: (req) => `${req.body?.email ?? ''}|${req.ip}` }), login()). Consider a stronger password hash (bcrypt/argon2) as a separate change.\n\nCWE-307. Severity MEDIUM, confidence high."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "routes/login.ts",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 50,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "res.status(401).send(res.__('Invalid email or password.'))"
                  }
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "login",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "login"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
