        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-639",
          "ruleIndex": 6,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Data export returns other customers' orders because orders are keyed by a vowel-masked email.\n\nOrders are stored with email.replace(/[aeiou]/gi, '*') (routes/order.ts:170) and the export looks them up by the same mask of the caller's email (line 22). Two accounts whose emails differ only in vowels share a key, so the export returns the other customer's orders. The lookup is not scoped by UserId.\n\nImpact: Cross-customer order history disclosure in the data export.\n\nExploit scenario: Victim email is visible on public reviews. The attacker registers a variant that differs only in vowels (for example victim jim@... vs jom@...), then POST /rest/user/data-export. The response includes the victim's orderId, totalPrice, products, bonus and eta. The captcha gate can be skipped (see the imageCaptcha finding).\n\nPreconditions: Victim email known (public in reviews); Attacker can register a vowel-variant email.\n\nRecommendation: Key orders on the stable user identity, not a display mask. Store UserId when the order is inserted (routes/order.ts:170) and query db.ordersCollection.find({ UserId: loggedInUser.data.id }) here. Backfill existing orders. The same masked-email lookup exists at routes/orderHistory.ts:16 and should be fixed in the same change.\n\nCWE-639. Severity MEDIUM, confidence high."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "routes/dataExport.ts",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 33,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "orders = await db.ordersCollection.find({ email: updatedEmail })"
                  }
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "dataExport",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "dataExport"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
