        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-200",
          "ruleIndex": 5,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Password reset response returns full user record including TOTP secret and password hash.\n\nresetPassword sends the updated Sequelize user instance as JSON; with no toJSON override, the response includes totpSecret and password. The same unfiltered serialization occurs at routes/changePassword.ts:56 and routes/saveLoginIp.ts:33, which return to the authenticated caller only.\n\nImpact: Two-factor authentication bypass for any account where the security answer is known, plus disclosure of the stored password hash.\n\nExploit scenario: Attacker who knows a victim email and security answer (the answer is guessable, see the reset-answer findings) posts /rest/user/reset-password. The response contains the victim TOTP seed, so the attacker can generate second-factor codes and log in after the reset.\n\nPreconditions: Attacker knows the victim email and security answer; Victim has 2FA enabled (otherwise the password reset alone is the takeover).\n\nRecommendation: Return an allowlisted projection, and make the model incapable of serializing secrets:\n\nres.json({ user: { id: user.id, email: user.email, username: user.username, role: user.role } })\n\nIn models/user.ts add toJSON() { const v = { ...this.get({ plain: true }) }; delete v.password; delete v.totpSecret; delete v.deluxeToken; return v }. Apply the same fix to changePassword.ts:56 and saveLoginIp.ts:33.\n\nCWE-200. Severity MEDIUM, confidence high."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "routes/resetPassword.ts",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 46,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "res.json({ user: updatedUser })"
                  }
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "resetPassword",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "resetPassword"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
