        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-200",
          "ruleIndex": 5,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Unauthenticated review listing exposes email addresses of every user who liked a review.\n\nGET /rest/products/:id/reviews is unauthenticated (server.ts:672). The handler returns full review documents, including likedBy, which the like route fills with raw user emails (likeProductReviews.ts:45). queryResultToJson only wraps the data (lib/utils.ts:26-34) and strips nothing.\n\nImpact: Disclosure of customer email addresses (PII) to unauthenticated callers. Review author emails are shown publicly by design, but likedBy is not displayed in the UI, so this exposure is additional.\n\nExploit scenario: An anonymous client GETs the reviews of any product and receives likedBy arrays containing plaintext customer emails. Iterating over products harvests a list of customer addresses for phishing.\n\nPreconditions: None: unauthenticated request.\n\nRecommendation: Strip likedBy before responding and keep the per-requester liked flag computed earlier: res.json(utils.queryResultToJson(reviews.map(({ likedBy, ...r }) => r))). Consider storing user ids instead of emails in likedBy.\n\nCWE-359. Severity MEDIUM, confidence high."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "routes/showProductReviews.ts",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 45,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "      res.json(utils.queryResultToJson(reviews))"
                  }
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "showProductReviews",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "showProductReviews"
                }
              ]
            }
