        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-306",
          "ruleIndex": 23,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Access and audit log files served without authentication.\n\n/support/logs and /support/logs/:file (server.ts:306-308) have no authentication. verify.accessControlChallenges (routes/verify.ts:64-79) only records challenge solves and then calls next(). The handler streams any file in logs/ with sendFile (line 14), and the log directory receives morgan 'combined' output (server.ts:362-370).\n\nImpact: Disclosure of client IP addresses, traffic patterns and any sensitive data placed in request URLs, including the password-in-query issue reported separately at changePassword.ts:14.\n\nExploit scenario: An anonymous client lists /support/logs and downloads /support/logs/access.log.<date>, which holds client IPs, user agents and full request URLs.\n\nPreconditions: None: unauthenticated request.\n\nRecommendation: Require authentication and an operator role on /support/logs before the index and file routes, for example app.use('/support/logs', security.isAuthorized(), <role check>). Alternatively move logs out of the served tree. Allowlist file names in the handler.\n\nCWE-306. Severity MEDIUM, confidence high."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "routes/logfileServer.ts",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
