        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-345",
          "ruleIndex": 11,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Discount coupons are z85-encoded, not authenticated; any customer can forge a coupon for any discount.\n\ngenerateCoupon produces z85.encode of MMMYY-discount with no MAC, and discountFromCoupon trusts z85.decode plus a month check, so the attacker's own encoding is accepted.\n\nImpact: Financial integrity loss: arbitrary discounts on orders for the current month.\n\nExploit scenario: The attacker z85-encodes NOV26-99 (or the current month) locally, applies it to their own basket with the PUT route, and places an order at about 1% of the price.\n\nPreconditions: An authenticated customer account.\n\nRecommendation: Authenticate coupons. Either store single-use coupon records server-side, or append an HMAC-SHA256 over the payload with a server secret and verify it with crypto.timingSafeEqual before applying the discount.\n\nCWE-345. Severity MEDIUM, confidence high."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "lib/insecurity.ts",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 106,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "  const decoded = z85.decode(coupon)"
                  }
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "discountFromCoupon",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "discountFromCoupon"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "claudeSecurityPlugin": {
              "id": "F52",
              "title": "Discount coupons are z85-encoded, not authenticated; any customer can forge a coupon for any discount",
