        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-345",
          "ruleIndex": 11,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Client-supplied base64 campaign coupon accepted with no authenticity check.\n\nreq.body.couponData is base64-decoded and split on '-' into a campaign code and a timestamp. Validity is checked only by equality with public constants (line 201), with no MAC and no server-side record. The else-if branch runs whenever the basket has no stored coupon (line 195). Any authenticated user can build WMNSDY2019-<validOn> and receive the campaign discount. The threat model files this as CWE-639; the defect under this lens is that the client supplies an unauthenticated discount token.\n\nImpact: Repeatable 40 to 75 percent discount on any order, bounded by the campaign table. Integrity of pricing.\n\nExploit scenario: A registered user base64-encodes 'WMNSDY2019-' followed by the validOn millisecond value from the public campaigns table (order.ts:210) and sends it as couponData in POST /rest/basket/:id/checkout with no stored basket coupon. The branch returns 75 (line 203) and the order is discounted. The same token can be reused on any order.\n\nPreconditions: Authenticated account (checkout sits behind isAuthorized at server.ts:431); Basket has no stored coupon, so the else-if branch is reached.\n\nRecommendation: Delete the else-if branch (order.ts:195-205) and the campaigns table. If campaign codes are a business requirement, store them server-side with validity windows and per-user redemption and look them up by code; never derive a discount from client input. Clamp any discount to 0-100 before use in calculateApplicableDiscount.\n\nCWE-345. Severity MEDIUM, confidence high."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "routes/order.ts",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 196,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "const couponData = Buffer.from(req.body.couponData, 'base64').toString().split('-')"
                  }
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "calculateApplicableDiscount",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "calculateApplicableDiscount"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "claudeSecurityPlugin": {
