        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-287",
          "ruleIndex": 3,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Client-controlled X-Forwarded-For defeats rate limits because trust proxy is enabled globally.\n\napp.enable('trust proxy') makes req.ip the leftmost X-Forwarded-For value supplied by the client, and the reset-password limiter keys on headers['X-Forwarded-For'] (a case-sensitive lookup that is always undefined in Node) and falls back to ip (server.ts:375-379); the 2FA limiters use the default req.ip (server.ts:491, 498, 504). Scope note: the limiter configuration is in server.ts.\n\nImpact: Rate limits on password reset and 2FA verification are ineffective, enabling brute force of security answers and TOTP codes and therefore account takeover. The Morty reset challenge is designed around this, but the flaw also applies to the 2FA limiters.\n\nExploit scenario: Attacker sends a different X-Forwarded-For value on every request. Each request gets a new limiter key, so the 100-per-5-minutes limit never triggers. This allows unlimited password-reset security-answer guessing and 6-digit TOTP brute force against /rest/2fa/verify.\n\nPreconditions: Attacker must know the target's password (for 2FA brute force) or security answer (for reset).\n\nRecommendation: Trust only the real proxy hop count, and key limiters on the socket address:\\n  app.set('trust proxy', 1) // or false when not behind a proxy\\n  keyGenerator: (req) => req.ip\\nRemove the custom keyGenerator that reads a header name that never matches.\n\nCWE-807. Severity MEDIUM, confidence high."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "server.ts",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 374,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "  app.enable('trust proxy')"
                  }
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "configureApp",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "configureApp"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "claudeSecurityPlugin": {
