        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-862",
          "ruleIndex": 16,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Any authenticated customer can list all user accounts and read any user record.\n\nGET /api/Users requires only a valid token (server.ts:395) and the finale list returns every row with only password and totpSecret excluded (server.ts:523); GET /api/Users/:id (server.ts:397) has no ownership check either. Scope note: server.ts glue.\n\nImpact: Bulk disclosure of personal data for all users (emails, login IPs, roles), enabling targeted phishing and credential attacks.\n\nExploit scenario: Any registered customer calls GET /api/Users to dump every account's email, role, lastLoginIp, profileImage and deluxeToken, then uses the list for phishing or credential stuffing.\n\nPreconditions: Any authenticated customer account.\n\nRecommendation: Restrict the list to admins and add a read.auth hook for by-id reads that requires the caller to be the owner or an admin:\\n  app.get('/api/Users', security.isAdmin())\\n  resource.read.auth((req, res, context) => { /* allow owner or admin only */ return context.continue })\\nAlso add lastLoginIp and deluxeToken to excludeAttributes for the User resource.\n\nCWE-862. Severity MEDIUM, confidence high."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "server.ts",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 395,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "  app.get('/api/Users', security.isAuthorized())"
                  }
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "configureApp",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "configureApp"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
