        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-862",
          "ruleIndex": 16,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Any authenticated user can list all customers' complaints.\n\nGET /api/Complaints requires only authentication (server.ts:413) and the finale list returns every Complaint row, which carries UserId (models/complaint.ts:19), while GET by id is denied (server.ts:415), which is inconsistent. Scope note: server.ts glue.\n\nImpact: Disclosure of other customers' complaint messages and linked user ids.\n\nExploit scenario: A customer calls GET /api/Complaints and reads the complaint text submitted by every other customer, which may include personal data and order details.\n\nPreconditions: Any authenticated customer account.\n\nRecommendation: Scope the list to the caller: app.get('/api/Complaints', security.appendUserId()) plus resource.list.fetch.before((req, res, context) => { context.criteria = { ...(context.criteria ?? {}), UserId: req.body.UserId }; return context.continue }). Also bind UserId on POST at server.ts:414 so complaints cannot be attributed to other users.\n\nCWE-862. Severity MEDIUM, confidence high."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "server.ts",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 413,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "  app.get('/api/Complaints', security.isAuthorized())"
                  }
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "configureApp",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "configureApp"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
