        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-862",
          "ruleIndex": 16,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Any authenticated customer can create catalog products, contrary to the 'only GET' comment.\n\nThe comment at server.ts:400 says only GET is allowed for products, but line 401 allows any authenticated user to POST, which reaches the finale create for Product (server.ts:524, 540-546). Scope note: server.ts glue.\n\nImpact: Customers can insert content into the shared catalog that all users see.\n\nExploit scenario: A customer creates products with arbitrary names, descriptions and prices. The products appear in the public catalog for all users, which is a spam or phishing vector and can carry stored XSS if rendered unsafely.\n\nPreconditions: Any authenticated customer account.\n\nRecommendation: Require admin for product creation: app.post('/api/Products', security.isAuthorized(), security.isAdmin()) using the isAdmin helper suggested for the PUT guard.\n\nCWE-862. Severity MEDIUM, confidence high."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "server.ts",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
