          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "XML external entity file disclosure through the deprecated .xml upload parser.\n\nAttacker XML from an unauthenticated upload is parsed with external-entity substitution and DTD loading enabled, with host filesystem input providers registered, and the expanded document is echoed back in the error response at line 83.\n\nImpact: Read of any file the Node process can read (config, data/juiceshop.sqlite, key material), limited to 400 characters per request by utils.trunc. Each request can read a different file.\n\nExploit scenario: POST /file-upload with a file named x.xml whose DTD defines an external entity pointing at a local path. The response error contains the first 400 characters of the expanded document, which discloses the file contents. Repeat for other files.\n\nPreconditions: deprecatedInterfaceChallenge enabled: disabledEnv Docker, Heroku, Windows; enabled on a native host in auto safety mode; No authentication required.\n\nRecommendation: The endpoint is deprecated, so do not parse the document at all. Return the 410 without parsing or echoing content, as the else branch does:\n\n  res.status(410)\n  next(new Error('B2B customer complaints via file upload have been deprecated for security reasons (' + file.originalname + ')'))\n\nIf parsing must remain, in lib/xml.ts use XML_PARSE_NONET without XML_PARSE_NOENT or XML_PARSE_DTDLOAD, and drop the xmlRegisterFsInputProviders() call at lib/xml.ts:22.\n\nCWE-611. Severity MEDIUM, confidence medium."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "routes/fileUpload.ts",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 80,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "const xmlString = await parseXmlString(data)"
                  }
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "handleXmlUpload",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "handleXmlUpload"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
