        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-862",
          "ruleIndex": 16,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Coupon issuance is gated only by the LLM system prompt and the discount is unbounded.\n\nThe generateCoupon tool runs for any unauthenticated caller of /rest/chat. Its execute handler calls security.generateCoupon(discount) (chat.ts:185) with an LLM-chosen value. The only controls are natural-language rules in the system prompt (chat.ts:98-103) and a schema with no bounds (chat.ts:180, z.number()). No server-side customer, order or policy check exists.\n\nImpact: Free or over-discounted orders, which is direct financial loss. A privileged business action (issuing discounts) is authorised by a language model rather than by server code, so policy is bypassed whenever the model is persuaded.\n\nExploit scenario: An anonymous user prompts the bot, or injects instructions into the conversation, to call generateCoupon with discount 100. The model complies and returns a valid code for the current month. Any customer then applies it with PUT /rest/basket/:id/coupon/:coupon and checks out at the discounted price.\n\nPreconditions: The model must comply with the injected request, which is non-deterministic (not executed here); A logged-in account is needed to redeem the code.\n\nRecommendation: Enforce the policy in code. Use discount: z.number().int().min(1).max(10). Require an authenticated customer (security.authenticatedUsers.from(req)). Check the damaged-order and return conditions server-side before calling security.generateCoupon. Bind coupons to a user and make them single-use. This removes the intended prompt-injection challenge behaviour.\n\nCWE-862. Severity MEDIUM, confidence medium."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "routes/chat.ts",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
