        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-552",
          "ruleIndex": 15,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "KeePass vault incident-support.kdbx is explicitly allowlisted for unauthenticated download.\n\nThe /ftp/:file route (server.ts:295) is public. The verify step adds an explicit exception for incident-support.kdbx, and the file is then sent from ftp/ (line 32). ftp/incident-support.kdbx exists in the tree. KeePass databases are encrypted, so the risk is offline cracking of the master password, not plaintext disclosure. The contents were not inspected. Also CWE-538: The route explicitly allows incident-support.kdbx, a password database, and sends it from the publicly served ftp/ directory.\n\nImpact: Unauthenticated access to a credential vault. Impact depends on master-password strength and what the vault holds.\n\nExploit scenario: An anonymous client downloads /ftp/incident-support.kdbx and tries offline cracking against the master password. If it is weak, any credentials stored in the vault are recovered.\n\nPreconditions: Offline cracking success depends on master-password strength.\n\nRecommendation: Remove the explicit exception and move the vault out of the public ftp/ tree. If a challenge needs it, serve it through an authenticated, role-gated route. This removes the intended challenge file. Also CWE-538: Remove the vault from the publicly served tree. Never serve credential stores from a web path, and rotate any credentials they contain.\n\nCWE-552. Severity MEDIUM, confidence medium."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "routes/fileServer.ts",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 26,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "    if (file && (endsWithAllowlistedFileType(file) || (file === 'incident-support.kdbx'))) {"
                  }
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "servePublicFiles",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "servePublicFiles"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
