              "line": 24,
              "description": "afterLogin passes the full Sequelize user record (including password MD5 and totpSecret) as the JWT payload; UserModel has no toJSON override (models/user.ts), so jwt.sign serializes both secrets into the token that is returned to the client and cached. The same pattern repeats at routes/updateUserProfile.ts:40, routes/deluxe.ts:48, routes/passkey.ts:66 and routes/2fa.ts:42.",
              "exploit_scenario": "Any party that obtains the token (XSS reading localStorage or the cookie, a leaked log or proxy record, a shared device) decodes the payload, takes the unsalted MD5 password hash for offline cracking and the TOTP seed to generate valid second-factor codes indefinitely, outliving session logout.",
