        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-307",
          "ruleIndex": 13,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "TOTP brute force is unthrottled because the per-IP limiter trusts spoofable X-Forwarded-For.\n\nThe /rest/2fa/verify handler checks the 6-digit TOTP code only behind an IP-keyed rate limiter, and the server sets trust proxy to true (server.ts:374), so req.ip comes from a client-supplied X-Forwarded-For. The handler itself has no per-account lockout and no replay protection. The handler is in routes/2fa.ts, not routes/verify.ts.\n\nImpact: Second factor is defeated after password compromise, giving full account takeover.\n\nExploit scenario: Attacker who knows the password obtains a tmpToken (valid 6h) from /rest/user/login, then sends TOTP guesses to /rest/2fa/verify while rotating X-Forwarded-For per request. The window has about three valid codes out of 10^6, so about 3e5 tries succeed on average, with no lockout.\n\nPreconditions: Attacker knows the victim password (2FA is the remaining barrier); Rate limiter keys on the spoofable client IP.\n\nRecommendation: Throttle per account, not per IP: key the limiter on the tmpToken user id, lock the tmpToken after N failures, and record the last-used TOTP counter to reject replays. Set trust proxy to the actual number of trusted hops instead of true:\n\napp.set('trust proxy', 1)\n\nrateLimit({ keyGenerator: (req) => String(security.decode(req.body.tmpToken)?.userId ?? req.ip) }).\n\nCWE-307. Severity MEDIUM, confidence medium."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "routes/2fa.ts",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 31,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "const isValid = verifySync({ secret: user.totpSecret, token: totpToken, epochTolerance: 30 }).valid"
                  }
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "verify",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "verify"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "claudeSecurityPlugin": {
              "id": "F68",
              "title": "TOTP brute force is unthrottled because the per-IP limiter trusts spoofable X-Forwarded-For",
              "impact": "Second factor is defeated after password compromise, giving full account takeover.",
