              "description": "The /rest/2fa/verify handler checks the 6-digit TOTP code only behind an IP-keyed rate limiter, and the server sets trust proxy to true (server.ts:374), so req.ip comes from a client-supplied X-Forwarded-For. The handler itself has no per-account lockout and no replay protection. The handler is in routes/2fa.ts, not routes/verify.ts.",
              "exploit_scenario": "Attacker who knows the password obtains a tmpToken (valid 6h) from /rest/user/login, then sends TOTP guesses to /rest/2fa/verify while rotating X-Forwarded-For per request. The window has about three valid codes out of 10^6, so about 3e5 tries succeed on average, with no lockout.",
              "preconditions": [
                "Attacker knows the victim password (2FA is the remaining barrier)",
