        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-1333",
          "ruleIndex": 27,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Quadratic-time regex on attacker-controlled username runs on every profile load (ReDoS).\n\nAn unanchored regex with a greedy .* after a literal prefix runs synchronously on the stored username, which can be attacker-sized up to the body limit.\n\nImpact: Availability: the whole server stalls per request, and one account can sustain the stall.\n\nExploit scenario: An authenticated user sets username to about 50k repeats of the two characters #{ (under the ~100 KB body limit) and then requests GET /profile repeatedly. Each #{ start position scans to the end of the string looking for }, which is O(n^2) overall, and the synchronous match blocks the single Node event loop for seconds per request.\n\nPreconditions: usernameXssChallenge enabled (not Docker or Heroku); An authenticated session via open self-registration.\n\nRecommendation: Remove the regex with the eval fix above. If any #{ handling is kept, check linear-time anchors instead, for example username.startsWith('#{') && username.endsWith('}'). Also cap username length (e.g. at most 255 characters) in routes/updateUserProfile.ts before user.update, and set a model-level len validator.\n\nCWE-1333. Severity MEDIUM, confidence medium."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "routes/userProfile.ts",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
