          "ruleId": "CWE-22",
          "ruleIndex": 10,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Local file read via request-controlled layout passed into template render locals.\n\nThe request body, including the layout field, is spread into res.render locals, where the template engine uses it as a layout path, and the only check is a substring blacklist on the enabled branch.\n\nImpact: Read of arbitrary files readable by the Node process, such as configuration, source and keys outside the three blacklisted substrings. Confidentiality is affected.\n\nExploit scenario: Log in or self-register, then POST /dataerasure with the token cookie and urlencoded body layout=../package.json (or a deeper ../ chain). When lfrChallenge is enabled, the blacklist only blocks paths containing ftp, ctf.key or encryptionkeys, and the callback returns the first 100 characters. When it is disabled (Docker or Heroku), the else branch at line 123 passes req.body with no check, and the full rendered output is returned.\n\nPreconditions: An authenticated session via open self-registration; hbs honours a 'layout' key in render locals and resolves relative paths. This is not verified: node_modules is absent, and the rationale relies on the project's own lfrChallenge design.\n\nRecommendation: Stop passing request data to render. Patch both branches so the locals contain only the trusted theme values, and remove the layout feature:\n\nres.render('dataErasureResult', { ...themeVars }, ...)\n\nIf a layout must be selectable, map a fixed enum to constant file names and never accept a path from the request. Keep the isForbiddenFile check only as a blacklist supplement, not as the control.\n\nCWE-22. Severity MEDIUM, confidence medium."
          },
          "locations": [
