        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-307",
          "ruleIndex": 13,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Security-answer guessing is unthrottled because the reset limiter keys on spoofable IP.\n\nThe answer comparison is reachable unauthenticated and is limited only by the reset-password limiter at server.ts:375-379. That limiter reads headers['X-Forwarded-For'] (capitalized, which never matches Node's lowercased headers) and otherwise falls back to req.ip, which trust proxy derives from the client-supplied X-Forwarded-For. The question is retrieved first from the unauthenticated /rest/user/security-question endpoint.\n\nImpact: Account takeover via recovery-question guessing for accounts with weak answers.\n\nExploit scenario: Attacker fetches the victim question, then tries answers from a dictionary against /rest/user/reset-password, rotating X-Forwarded-For to avoid the limiter. On a match the password is reset.\n\nPreconditions: Victim has a guessable security answer; Limiter remains bypassable as configured.\n\nRecommendation: Throttle per account plus IP and lock the account after a small number of wrong answers. Fix the limiter key to read req.headers['x-forwarded-for'] only behind a known proxy, or ignore it. Compare with timingSafeEqual on fixed-length digests.\n\nCWE-307. Severity MEDIUM, confidence medium."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "routes/resetPassword.ts",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 41,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "if ((data != null) && security.hmac(answer) === data.answer) {"
                  }
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "resetPassword",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "resetPassword"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
