        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-203",
          "ruleIndex": 29,
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Unauthenticated security-question lookup reveals whether an account exists and discloses its question.\n\nThe endpoint responds with the security question object for an existing account and with an empty object otherwise. The difference is an account-existence oracle. The question text also tells an attacker which answer to guess, which feeds the reset-password brute force.\n\nImpact: Account enumeration and disclosure of each user's security question, which narrows guessing for reset-password.\n\nExploit scenario: Attacker calls GET /rest/user/security-question?email=<candidate> for many addresses. Responses containing a question mark the address as a registered account and reveal the question to target.\n\nPreconditions: None (unauthenticated).\n\nRecommendation: Return the same shape for known and unknown emails. For unknown emails, return a decoy question chosen deterministically from the email (for example from a fixed list keyed by a hash of the email) so the response does not reveal existence. Also rate-limit this endpoint.\n\nCWE-204. Severity LOW, confidence high."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "routes/securityQuestion.ts",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
