        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-347",
          "ruleIndex": 4,
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Chatbot resolves caller identity from an unverified JWT payload.\n\nPOST /rest/chat is unauthenticated (server.ts:678). getUserId takes the Bearer token and passes it to security.decode, which is jws.decode with no signature check (insecurity.ts:56). The decoded data.id then drives the username lookup (chat.ts:52) and the getOrderById tool (chat.ts:163-170).\n\nImpact: Identity spoofing toward the chatbot with no credential. Discloses other users' usernames and, when an order ID is known, that user's order details. Bounded because order IDs are md5(email)[0:4] plus 16 random hex characters (routes/order.ts:40), so they are not enumerable.\n\nExploit scenario: An attacker sends Authorization: Bearer <header>.<base64url of {\"data\":{\"id\":N}}>.x to /rest/chat with any signature. The server treats the caller as user N, places that user's username into the system prompt, and lets the getOrderById tool return orders matching user N's masked email for any order ID the attacker holds. Looping over N enumerates usernames.\n\nPreconditions: Username disclosure needs nothing beyond a numeric user id; Order-detail disclosure additionally needs the target order ID.\n\nRecommendation: Use the server-side session instead of the token payload: const user = security.authenticatedUsers.from(req); return user?.data?.id. Or verify first with jwt.verify(token, publicKey, { algorithms: ['RS256'] }) before reading claims. Apply the same change to getUserNameFromToken and to the aiDebuggingChallenge role read.\n\nCWE-347. Severity LOW, confidence high."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "routes/chat.ts",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 45,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "  const decoded = security.decode(token) as { data?: { id?: number } } | undefined"
                  }
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "getUserId",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "getUserId"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "claudeSecurityPlugin": {
              "id": "F77",
              "title": "Chatbot resolves caller identity from an unverified JWT payload",
