          "ruleId": "CWE-312",
          "ruleIndex": 30,
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "TOTP seed stored in cleartext in the user table.\n\nsetup stores the new TOTP secret directly in the Users row. Anyone who can read the database can clone the second factor. The seed also appears in plaintext in the session payload (see the login JWT finding).\n\nImpact: Second factor cloneable by anyone with database read access.\n\nExploit scenario: Attacker with read access to the Users table (backup, SQL injection read, replica) takes totpSecret for each enrolled user and generates valid codes.\n\nPreconditions: Attacker has database read access.\n\nRecommendation: Encrypt the seed at rest with AES-256-GCM using a key from the environment, and decrypt in verify, setup and disable:\n\nuserModel.totpSecret = encryptSecret(secret)\n\nMigrate existing rows on next login.\n\nCWE-312. Severity LOW, confidence high."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "routes/2fa.ts",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
