        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-362",
          "ruleIndex": 31,
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Check-then-act race lets one user like the same review many times.\n\nThe already-liked check (line 31) reads likedBy once. The unconditional $inc (lines 35-38) runs before likedBy is updated, and likedBy is only written after a 150 ms sleep (lines 41-53). Concurrent or closely spaced requests from the same user all pass the check.\n\nImpact: Vote inflation on the like counter and bypass of the one-like-per-user rule. Bounded to that counter.\n\nExploit scenario: One account sends about 20 parallel POST /rest/products/reviews requests for the same review id. Each passes the check, likesCount rises by up to 20 and likedBy can hold duplicate entries.\n\nPreconditions: A registered account (isAuthorized at server.ts:675).\n\nRecommendation: Use one conditional atomic update: db.reviewsCollection.update({ _id: id, likedBy: { $ne: user.data.email } }, { $inc: { likesCount: 1 }, $push: { likedBy: user.data.email } }), and reject when modified is 0. Confirm that marsdb supports those operators. Otherwise serialise per review with a mutex. Remove the artificial sleep.\n\nCWE-362. Severity LOW, confidence high."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "routes/likeProductReviews.ts",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 37,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "        { $inc: { likesCount: 1 } }"
                  }
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "likeProductReviews",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "likeProductReviews"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
