          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Coupon endpoint updates any basket by id with no owner check.\n\napplyCoupon fetches the basket with findByPk(id) and then calls basket.update({ coupon }). Nothing compares the basket's UserId to the requester, so any authenticated user can set or clear the coupon on another user's basket. An invalid code also clears the victim's existing coupon (coupon.ts:16, 24).\n\nImpact: Tampering with another user's discount state. Low, since it does not expose data or move money directly.\n\nExploit scenario: Attacker sends PUT /rest/basket/<victim id>/coupon/<any code> to replace or clear the victim's coupon.\n\nPreconditions: Any registered account.\n\nRecommendation: Scope the lookup to the requester: `const basket = await BasketModel.findOne({ where: { id, UserId: req.body.UserId } }); if (!basket) return next(new Error(...))`.\n\nCWE-639. Severity LOW, confidence high."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "routes/coupon.ts",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 18,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "const basket = await BasketModel.findByPk(id)"
                  }
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "applyCoupon",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "applyCoupon"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
