          "ruleIndex": 6,
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Anonymous recycle lookup by id, including arrays, reveals other users' recycle records.\n\ngetRecycleItem parses the path id with JSON.parse (line 14) and queries by it without authentication or ownership, so an array id returns many rows.\n\nImpact: Anonymous enumeration of recycle requests and linkage to user and address ids.\n\nExploit scenario: GET /api/Recycles/[1,2,3,...] returns recycle records with user, address and quantity IDs.\n\nPreconditions: none.\n\nRecommendation: Require auth and scope by UserId; accept only integer ids (Number.parseInt with validation).\n\nCWE-639. Severity LOW, confidence high."
          },
