        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-1333",
          "ruleIndex": 27,
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Quadratic regex on attacker-controlled profileImage runs on every profile load in all deployments.\n\nsolveIf evaluates its criteria whenever the challenge is unsolved, without checking disabledEnv, so this regex on the attacker-set profileImage runs even in Docker.\n\nImpact: Bounded availability impact (sub-second to about a second per request) that one account can repeat.\n\nExploit scenario: POST /profile/image/url with imageUrl set to an unresolvable http URL followed by about 8,000 copies of ';script-src'. The fetch fails and the raw string is stored. Each GET /profile then runs the greedy (.)* scan once per ';script-src', which is roughly O(n^2) and takes around a second per request.\n\nPreconditions: An authenticated session via open self-registration; usernameXssChallenge not yet solved on the instance.\n\nRecommendation: Replace the regex with a linear check and gate the predicate with utils.isChallengeEnabled as line 57 does: const img = user?.profileImage ?? ''; return username && /;\\s*script-src/.test(img) && img.includes(\"'unsafe-inline'\") && username.includes('<script>alert(`xss`)</script>'). Also cap profileImage length in routes/profileImageUrlUpload.ts.\n\nCWE-1333. Severity LOW, confidence medium."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "routes/userProfile.ts",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 94,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "return username && user?.profileImage.match(/;[ ]*script-src(.)*'unsafe-inline'/g) !== null && username.includes('<script>alert(`xss`)</script>')"
                  }
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "getUserProfile",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "getUserProfile"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "claudeSecurityPlugin": {
              "id": "F86",
              "title": "Quadratic regex on attacker-controlled profileImage runs on every profile load in all deployments",
              "impact": "Bounded availability impact (sub-second to about a second per request) that one account can repeat.",
              "file": "routes/userProfile.ts",
              "line": 94,
              "description": "solveIf evaluates its criteria whenever the challenge is unsolved, without checking disabledEnv, so this regex on the attacker-set profileImage runs even in Docker.",
