        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-352",
          "ruleIndex": 32,
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Cookie-authenticated profile update has no anti-CSRF protection.\n\nPOST /profile authenticates from the token cookie and changes state (username) with no CSRF token or origin check beyond the training challenge. The cookie is set without a SameSite attribute (updateUserProfile.ts:42, lib/insecurity.ts:192), and express.urlencoded (server.ts:339) accepts form posts. Browsers without Lax-by-default for cookies (for example Firefox or Safari) send the cookie on a cross-site form POST. Chrome's default largely mitigates this, so exploitability is browser-dependent. The same pattern applies to POST /dataerasure (routes/dataErasure.ts:76-88).\n\nImpact: Unauthorized username change on a victim account. Integrity impact is low, and an attacker can use it to re-label accounts.\n\nExploit scenario: Attacker hosts an auto-submitting form that POSTs username=<attacker value> to /profile. A victim who visits the page in a browser that sends the token cookie has their username changed, and receives a fresh token cookie.\n\nPreconditions: Victim is logged in in a browser that sends the cookie on cross-site POST; Victim visits attacker page.\n\nRecommendation: Set SameSite=Lax (or Strict) on the token cookie (res.cookie('token', token, { sameSite: 'strict' })), and require a CSRF token or enforce Origin/Sec-Fetch-Site checks on state-changing cookie-authenticated routes (/profile POST, /dataerasure POST). Make the cookie httpOnly if the frontend does not read it from JavaScript.\n\nCWE-352. Severity LOW, confidence medium."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "routes/updateUserProfile.ts",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 17,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "const loggedInUser = security.authenticatedUsers.get(req.cookies.token)"
                  }
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "updateUserProfile",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "updateUserProfile"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "claudeSecurityPlugin": {
              "id": "F87",
              "title": "Cookie-authenticated profile update has no anti-CSRF protection",
              "impact": "Unauthorized username change on a victim account. Integrity impact is low, and an attacker can use it to re-label accounts.",
