              "description": "POST /profile authenticates from the token cookie and changes state (username) with no CSRF token or origin check beyond the training challenge. The cookie is set without a SameSite attribute (updateUserProfile.ts:42, lib/insecurity.ts:192), and express.urlencoded (server.ts:339) accepts form posts. Browsers without Lax-by-default for cookies (for example Firefox or Safari) send the cookie on a cross-site form POST. Chrome's default largely mitigates this, so exploitability is browser-dependent. The same pattern applies to POST /dataerasure (routes/dataErasure.ts:76-88).",
              "exploit_scenario": "Attacker hosts an auto-submitting form that POSTs username=<attacker value> to /profile. A victim who visits the page in a browser that sends the token cookie has their username changed, and receives a fresh token cookie.",
              "preconditions": [
