        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-732",
          "ruleIndex": 33,
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Session token cookie set without HttpOnly, Secure or SameSite.\n\nThe bearer session token is written to a cookie with default attributes, so scripts can read it and no SameSite restriction applies to the cookie that this same endpoint uses for authentication (line 17). lib/insecurity.ts:192 does the same on every authenticated request.\n\nImpact: Session token exposure to script and weaker CSRF protection on cookie-authenticated endpoints. The token is also stored in localStorage, so the incremental risk is limited.\n\nExploit scenario: Any script running on the origin, for example via XSS, reads document.cookie and exfiltrates the token. Cross-site POSTs to /profile can carry the cookie where SameSite defaults allow it.\n\nPreconditions: XSS on the origin or a browser that sends the cookie cross-site.\n\nRecommendation: Set cookie attributes explicitly:\n\nres.cookie('token', updatedToken, { httpOnly: true, sameSite: 'strict', secure: process.env.NODE_ENV === 'production' })\n\nApply the same in lib/insecurity.ts:192. Check that frontend code does not read this cookie via document.cookie before enabling httpOnly.\n\nCWE-1004. Severity LOW, confidence medium."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "routes/updateUserProfile.ts",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 42,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "res.cookie('token', updatedToken)"
                  }
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "updateUserProfile",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "updateUserProfile"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "claudeSecurityPlugin": {
