        },
        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-770",
          "ruleIndex": 22,
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Unbounded Prometheus label cardinality from client-controlled upload Content-Type.\n\nfile.mimetype (taken from the multipart part's client-supplied Content-Type) is used as a counter label on every upload, and prom-client keeps each distinct value as a permanent series.\n\nImpact: Gradual memory exhaustion (availability) of the server process. No direct confidentiality or integrity impact.\n\nExploit scenario: Send many uploads each with a unique Content-Type value. Each produces a new permanent time series, so process memory grows without bound.\n\nPreconditions: No authentication (POST /file-upload, server.ts:341).\n\nRecommendation: Map the value to a fixed set, falling back to 'other':\n\n  const KNOWN_MIME = new Set(['application/pdf', 'application/xml', 'text/xml', 'application/zip', 'application/x-yaml', 'text/yaml', 'application/x-zip-compressed'])\n  const label = KNOWN_MIME.has(file.mimetype) ? file.mimetype : 'other'\n  res.statusCode < 400 ? fileUploadsCountMetric.labels(label).inc() : fileUploadErrorsMetric.labels(label).inc().\n\nCWE-770. Severity LOW, confidence medium."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "routes/metrics.ts",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
