        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-770",
          "ruleIndex": 22,
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Unbounded cache keyed by request path parameter, with a synchronous directory read per new key.\n\nreadFixes caches an entry for every attacker-chosen key, including keys that match no file (line 42), and calls readdirSync (line 25) on each new key.\n\nImpact: Gradual memory growth and event-loop blocking (availability). No confidentiality or integrity impact.\n\nExploit scenario: Request many distinct /snippets/fixes/<random> keys. Each creates a permanent CodeFixes entry and a blocking readdirSync call, growing memory and slowing the event loop.\n\nPreconditions: No authentication (GET /snippets/fixes/:key, server.ts:712; POST /snippets/fixes, server.ts:713).\n\nRecommendation: Only cache keys that exist: check the key against the known challenge keys first and return 404 before writing CodeFixes[key]. Use Object.create(null) or a Map to avoid inherited-property hits.\n\nCWE-770. Severity LOW, confidence medium."
          },
          "locations": [
