        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-209",
          "ruleIndex": 34,
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "errorhandler returns stack traces to clients when NODE_ENV is unset.\n\napp.use(errorhandler()) (server.ts:722) falls back to development mode when NODE_ENV is unset, and neither the Dockerfile nor package.json sets NODE_ENV, so any request that triggers an error (for example malformed JSON that fails JSON.parse in the jsonParser at server.ts:355) returns a stack trace to an anonymous client. Scope note: server.ts glue.\n\nImpact: Information disclosure of server internals that aids further attacks. Limited in scope.\n\nExploit scenario: Attacker sends Content-Type application/json with an invalid body and reads the returned stack trace, which shows file paths, module versions and internal layout.\n\nPreconditions: NODE_ENV not set to production (the default when unset).\n\nRecommendation: Set NODE_ENV=production in the image and runtime, and configure the handler explicitly: app.use(errorhandler({ env: process.env.NODE_ENV ?? 'production' })). Mount the development handler only in development.\n\nCWE-209. Severity LOW, confidence medium."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "server.ts",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 722,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "  app.use(errorhandler())"
                  }
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "configureApp",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "configureApp"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
